{
 "encounter_id": "00870",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello, doctor. It's my fingers. They go tingly when I'm typing. And sometimes at night. Where was I? Oh, yes, the right hand, mostly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take your time. Which fingers are affected?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The thumb, the next two fingers. Not the little one."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long has this been happening?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About two months. It started when I took on the extra work. I type all day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does it wake you up at night?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, the fingers go numb, and I shake my hand to get them back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any weakness, dropping things?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I dropped a mug last week. And my grip feels weak."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pain in the neck, or down the arm?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. No neck pain. Just the hand."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "None."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any other conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "An underactive thyroid."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My wisdom teeth, a few years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse and temperature first. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70, temperature 36.5.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fine. Now, I'm going to tap on your wrist, and I'd like you to bend your wrist for a minute.",
   "pause": 40.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh! There, the tingling! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That brings on your symptoms, and the muscle at the base of your thumb is slightly weaker on the right."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What is it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "This looks like carpal tunnel syndrome, a squeezed nerve at the wrist, but I can't rule out a neck cause, or low thyroid levels contributing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Do I need an operation? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not yet. Most people improve with a wrist splint worn at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Where do I get one? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The pharmacy, or I can arrange it. And I'd like to arrange a blood test, to check your thyroid and sugar."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take breaks from typing every half hour, keep your wrist straight, and check your desk set-up."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If it doesn't improve in six weeks, or you get constant numbness or weakness, I'll arrange nerve tests and a specialist review."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
